  "details": "The VRChat status message has a built in censor/profanity filter---unfortunately, it doesn't work terribly well, at times, and can result in false positives.\nI had a status message set of \"oh my gosh, it's the Thing.\"\nThis got censored to \"ohmypoopsthething\"\nHilarious? ABSOLUTELY. Needless to say, I kinda doubt that \"gosh, it's\" or anything that ends in \"sh\" followed by \"it's\" should wind up censored. It also shouldn't jam all the characters together and lowercase them, either.\nI really think there's a compromise that likely should be had here. I know people find ever more creative ways to circumvent basic profanity filters, but typical, normal, non-offensive statements shouldn't be caught as false positives.",
